-- the production read path and kept as test-only fixtures.
--
-- LOCAL DEV ONLY, enforced by the guard below rather than assumed. Note
-- `supabase db reset` is NOT local-only: it accepts `--linked` and
-- `--db-url`, and `--no-seed` exists because seeding is the default after a
-- reset. Nothing in CI or the deploy path runs it against a remote, but a
-- mistyped flag would, so the guard refuses any database holding real users.
-- It is committed in the same change that flips `[db.seed] enabled = true`,
-- because config.toml's own comment warns that enabling the flag while the
