-- ── LOCAL-ONLY GUARD ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Aborts the whole seed (inside the transaction, so nothing is written) if
-- this database holds any auth user other than the dev account.
--
-- `supabase db reset` DOES accept `--linked` and `--db-url`, and ships
-- `--no-seed` precisely because seeding is the default after a reset — so
-- the comments that used to claim a seed cannot reach a remote project were
-- simply wrong. Below this line is an email-confirmed account whose password
-- is committed in plaintext; applying it to a project with real users would
-- create a working production login. A fresh local stack has no other users,
-- so this is invisible in normal use.
do $$
begin
  if exists (
    select 1 from auth.users
    where id <> '00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000d15c'::uuid
